//
// A NULLABLE NARROW RECEIVER INTO A DENSE METHOD IS REFUSED (`@FR-F-Recv` crossed with
// `@FR-N-Store`).  F-Recv: "a `τ?` receiver reaching `m(τ)` is (N-Store)'s case and warns" when
// only the dense method is declared.  N-Store makes that store a WARNING for most τ and a hard
// ERROR for a narrow width (u8…u32), where the null collides with a real value.  The cells
// beside this rule measure the warning on a struct receiver; this one moves the receiver to
// `u8?`, where the same case must be the error.
//
// @EXPECT_ERROR: a nullable `u8?` cannot be stored into parameter 1 of `fu`
//
// @falsified-at: none — a conformance guard; the refusal fires on 18594597b, interpret and native.
// CHANNEL: the compile diagnostic.
// ARMED: no instrument.
// WITNESS: the diagnostic names the receiver slot and the method.
// HOLDS: `a-nullable-narrow-receiver-reaches-its-nullable-twin` beside it.

fn fu(self: u8) -> integer { self + 1 }

fn main() {
  b: u8? = 7;
  assert(b.fu() == 8, "unreachable");
}
